{"ok":false,"profile":"vhutshilo","error":"The manuscript failed semantic validation (semantic_grounding_block).","semanticAudit":[{"candidateId":"semantic_grounding_block:8bf3ecb712c59457","disposition":"REJECT","reasonCode":"unsupported_comparison","ruleCode":"semantic_grounding_block","path":"EXECUTIVE-ASSESSMENT-POSITION.paragraphs[0]","blueprintPath":"EXECUTIVE-ASSESSMENT-POSITION","chapterTitle":"Executive assessment","sectionTitle":"Overall readiness position","span":"The assessment records an overall fraud-readiness score of 43.33 out of 100 and places the organisation at a Developing maturity. That score reflects a mix of partly designed and informal controls across several core domains rather than a uniformly weak baseline. The most useful relative foundation in the profile is the whistleblowing and reporting domain, which scores notably higher than other areas and therefore represents a comparatively stronger position on employee reporting and channel awareness. At the same time, material weaknesses appear in digital and identity risk, fraud-risk identification, operational fraud controls, detection capability and continuous improvement, all of which reduce the organisation’s capacity to prevent, detect and contain fraud across value-bearing processes."},{"candidateId":"semantic_grounding_block:8173c27ab585172c","disposition":"REPAIR","reasonCode":"repairable_overstatement","ruleCode":"semantic_grounding_block","path":"EXECUTIVE-ASSESSMENT-TAKEAWAY.paragraphs[0]","blueprintPath":"EXECUTIVE-ASSESSMENT-TAKEAWAY","chapterTitle":"Executive assessment","sectionTitle":"What this means for management","span":"Management should treat the assessed position as a targeted signal: a workable component exists in the reporting channel and that comparative strength can be used to accelerate improvement, but the score shows the need to connect governance, identity controls, supplier verification, detection and evidence processes into an owned programme. Immediate priorities are to establish process-by-process fraud mapping with named treatment owners; to ensure supplier activations and bank-detail changes receive independent verification; to reconcile and recertify privileged and role-based access; to define monitoring and escalation rules and evidence-preservation routes; and to approve an accountable executive mandate and review cadence that sustains delivery. Progress against these actions will materially alter the organisation’s ability to prevent value diversion, detect unusual activity and preserve case evidence."},{"candidateId":"semantic_grounding_block:ded4fc9bb5039548","disposition":"REJECT","reasonCode":"unsupported_structure","ruleCode":"semantic_grounding_block","path":"PRIORITY-FRAUD-EXPOSURES-CLUSTER-02.paragraphs[0]","blueprintPath":"PRIORITY-FRAUD-EXPOSURES-CLUSTER-02","chapterTitle":"Priority fraud exposures","sectionTitle":"Weak challenge at identity, transaction and sensitive-change points","span":"Controls over privileged and ordinary access and over monitoring are reported as partly designed or informal. That reported condition means sensitive, administrator or emergency accounts may be usable without a current business justification, robust logging, or periodic independent recertification. Similarly, analytics and rule-based detection are only partly designed and may not cover every priority fraud scenario."},{"candidateId":"semantic_grounding_block:7bc1c2f832eb102f","disposition":"REJECT","reasonCode":"unsupported_structure","ruleCode":"semantic_grounding_block","path":"PRIORITY-FRAUD-EXPOSURES-CLUSTER-02.paragraphs[1]","blueprintPath":"PRIORITY-FRAUD-EXPOSURES-CLUSTER-02","chapterTitle":"Priority fraud exposures","sectionTitle":"Weak challenge at identity, transaction and sensitive-change points","span":"When privileged or ordinary access is excessive and detection rules are incomplete, unusual approvals, manual adjustments or administrator actions can occur without timely review. A defined monitoring cycle, a rule catalogue that maps tests to scenarios, named reviewers and a formal escalation path are the completion criteria for remediating this exposure; absent them, unusual activity may not be challenged in time."}],"manuscriptDiagnostics":{"stage":"validate_manuscript","dispatchOccurred":true,"requestedProvider":"openai","requestedModel":"openai/gpt-5-mini","generationId":"gen_01M0T6223D4N50AKB8F4V59VB3","inputTokens":125221,"outputTokens":13333,"reasoningTokens":9024,"visibleOutputTokens":4309,"totalTokens":138554,"providerCostMicros":48525,"finishReason":"stop","manuscriptProviderCalls":1,"semanticReviewProviderCalls":2,"totalProviderCalls":3,"modelSelectionSource":"compiled_primary","providerAttemptRecords":[{"logicalStage":"manuscript","attempt":1,"modelAttempt":1,"model":"openai/gpt-5-mini","provider":"openai","primaryOrFallback":"primary","miniAttempt":1,"startedAt":"2026-08-24T15:26:09.447Z","endedAt":"2026-08-24T15:26:57.177Z","elapsedMs":47730,"generationId":"gen_01M0T6223D4N50AKB8F4V59VB3","responseId":"aitxt-YIBBr2yOfgdb8NJrUWhBOyp7","inputTokens":41101,"outputTokens":4026,"reasoningTokens":896,"visibleOutputTokens":3130,"totalTokens":45127,"providerCostMicros":18327,"finishReason":"stop","providerRequestDispatched":true,"success":true},{"logicalStage":"semantic_review","attempt":1,"modelAttempt":1,"model":"openai/gpt-5-mini","provider":"openai","primaryOrFallback":"primary","miniAttempt":1,"maxOutputTokens":4500,"startedAt":"2026-08-24T15:26:57.201Z","endedAt":"2026-08-24T15:27:48.732Z","elapsedMs":51531,"generationId":"gen_01M0T63GPPY7EBGB6J9Y2PREDZ","responseId":"aitxt-kPsX1AW4cBlIehiAEYqQ9vuE","inputTokens":42060,"outputTokens":4500,"reasoningTokens":3968,"visibleOutputTokens":532,"totalTokens":46560,"providerCostMicros":19515,"finishReason":"length","providerRequestDispatched":true,"success":false,"failureClassification":"retryable_technical","failureCode":"semantic_output_contract_too_large"},{"logicalStage":"semantic_review","attempt":2,"modelAtt